 status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAZAWA, FUMIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANO, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, NOBUYASU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>To measure the range of shade sheltered from scanning light, a comparator compares the output from a photodetector element with a threshold established by an MPU. The range where the former is smaller than the latter is measured to be a shadow. During a cycle of optical scanning, the threshold is varied in two or more steps depending on the scanning angle. The position and size of a pointing object such as a finger or pen are determined by measuring the shade sheltered from the scanning light.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Pour évaluer l'envergure de l'ombre non affectée par une lumière de balayage, un comparateur compare le niveau de sortie d'un élément photodétecteur avec un seuil établi par microprocesseur. On évalue comme étant une ombre la plage dans laquelle le niveau de sortie est inférieur au seuil. Durant un cycle de balayage optique, on fait varier le seuil selon deux ou plus de deux étapes en fonction de l'angle de balayage. La position et la taille d'un objet de pointage du type doigt ou stylo sont déterminées grâce à une évaluation de l'ombre non affectée par la lumière de balayage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set 